From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] d/steamvr_lh: convert pose time offset from seconds to nanoseconds

DriverPose_t::poseTimeOffset is expressed in seconds relative to the driver's
PoseUpdated call. The relation history uses nanoseconds, so convert with 1e9
instead of 1e6. Keep the offset and timestamp signed to support past poses
without converting a negative floating-point offset to an unsigned integer.

This changes only the pose timestamp conversion. Prediction limits and
skeletal root handling are unchanged. User hardware testing found no notable
fly-out improvement from this unit correction alone.
---
 src/xrt/drivers/steamvr_lh/device.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/xrt/drivers/steamvr_lh/device.cpp b/src/xrt/drivers/steamvr_lh/device.cpp
--- a/src/xrt/drivers/steamvr_lh/device.cpp
+++ b/src/xrt/drivers/steamvr_lh/device.cpp
@@ -1206,7 +1206,9 @@
-	const uint64_t ts = chrono_timestamp_ns() + static_cast<uint64_t>(newPose.poseTimeOffset * 1000000.0);
+	// OpenVR poseTimeOffset is in seconds; relation history timestamps are in nanoseconds.
+	const int64_t pose_time_offset_ns = static_cast<int64_t>(newPose.poseTimeOffset * 1000000000.0);
+	const int64_t ts = chrono_timestamp_ns() + pose_time_offset_ns;
 
 	m_relation_history_push(relation_hist, &relation, ts);
 }
 
 vr::ETrackedPropertyError
 Device::handle_properties(const vr::PropertyWrite_t *batch, uint32_t count)
